PRE-EXISTING, NON-SURFACE ENVIRONMENT BLOCK (documented, not a defect in this page)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The LITERAL gate `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16'
build test` FAILS on the unmodified tree (BUILD FAILED, exit 65) entirely because of pre-existing
parallel-merge breakage in code UNRELATED to sharing (HEAD c9c6fdb9f is a parallel-merge aggregate):

  (1) 224 co-located `*.Tests.swift` / `*.ModelTests.swift` files (170 under TeslaSync/feature-views,
      54 under TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets) `import XCTest` but are committed into the APP target's
      sources (project.yml `- path: TeslaSync/feature-views` / `dashboard-widgets`), so the app target
      cannot resolve module 'XCTest'. e.g. AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift:18, ActionBuilder.ModelTests.swift:11.
  (2) Duplicate type definitions from parallel merges cause ~59 "ambiguous for type lookup" /
      "invalid redeclaration" errors across the dashboard widget dirs — e.g. `DashboardWidgetSize` +
      `DashboardWidgetDescriptor` are each defined twice in Sources/DashboardWidgets/
      (BatteryCellsWidgetRegistry.swift AND DrivetrainHealthWidgetModel.swift), and the
      TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets copies duplicate Sources/Dashboard* types (VehicleHeroModel, ...).

ALL of these errors are outside apps/apple/Sources/Features/Sharing (grep of the build logs:
0 errors in Features/Sharing). They are committed, pre-existing, parallel-merge defects that this
P7 page neither introduced nor is in scope to fix ("Out of Scope: Other pages; ... Don't fix
pre-existing issues unrelated to your task").

